=== ARTICLE: Anatomy Servitron - how it is built ===
[size=5][b]How Anatomy Servitron is built[/b][/size]
A Servitron is a machine, so every part here is meant to look made: rubber, latex and metal, fitted the way a workshop would fit them. This is how each part was built, from the commits in the Anatomy repository (October 2026).

[size=4][b]The chest: rubber breasts in a machined socket[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Rubber, not skin.[/b] The breasts use a material built from Servitron's own rubber abdomen (its gloss and environment map) on a dark rubber texture, with CBBE's normal map for relief.[/*]
[*][b]The areola and nipple.[/b] A latex areola with a satin finish, placed on the texture's own painted areola, and a metal-capped nipple, in our own normal and specular maps (smooth rubber, glossier metal). Nothing comes from a skin mod.[/*]
[*][b]The socket.[/b] Where each breast meets the chest, a fillet runs from the breast's rim into the suit: a polished bead, a groove, an ease down to the suit's depth and a tuck. The band past the bead is the suit's own woven fabric (its colour, shine and weave).[/*]
[*][b]The suit behind it.[/b] The suit is pushed 3 units back behind the breasts, fading out past their outline, instead of being cut: cutting opened holes, because the suit is the chest's only wall. The front chest plate is removed. Under Silhouette's 365 body templates the suit stays behind the breasts in 325 (it was 183).[/*]
[*][b]Physics.[/b] The installer offers CBBE or 3BBB torsos. The 3BBB ones carry the same suit push and socket, so the breasts move with a 3BBB preset too.[/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]The openings: Servitron's rubber abdomens, rigged[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Rings that stretch and wrap.[/b] The rubber abdomens' openings are weighted to Anatomy's ring bones. With the Anatomy Engine 1.2.14 they open round what enters, and the canal wraps the shaft with 6 rings of 8 bones that close behind it.[/*]
[*][b]Each ring opens whole.[/b] The suit around the rings takes the stretch, so a ring opens as one piece instead of smearing into the suit (Anatomy Servitron 1.0.1).[/*]
[*][b]Aimed in every animation.[/b] Robots were never in the engine's list of people in a scene, so the aim never turned a shaft onto her rings. Servitrons are now on that list.[/*]
[*][b]AAF finds her.[/b] AAF's own Robot group lists only vanilla robots, so its scene wizard never offered a Servitron. She is added through her robot keyword and race.[/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]The male module: the abdomen decides[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Two modules at the Robot Workbench:[/b] GITS Rubber (Male) and Wetsuit Rubber (Male). The vagina is capped, the anus is kept, and a segmented latex penis with a flared base and its own balls sits on the skeleton's own Penis_00 to Penis_05 bones, so the engine aims it like any penis.[/*]
[*][b]The role follows the abdomen.[/b] A Rubber abdomen is a woman to AAF, a Male abdomen a man, and a closed suit keeps the robot out of scenes. Swap the abdomen and the role changes with it.[/*]
[*][b]A light plugin.[/b] AnatomyServitron.esp is flagged light: the two modules and their recipes.[/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]With our other mods[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Rapport[/b] 0.2.17+: a robot has no mouth, so Rapport never picks acts that need hers. 0.2.18 gives her a borrowed human voice by her role until a robot voiceover exists.[/*]
[*][b]Overture[/b] 0.2.0+: press R on a Servitron and she always says yes; her lines follow the body she is built with.[/*]
[*][b]Silhouette[/b] 0.3.7+: Servitrons get body shapes, and with this mod their breasts follow them while the suit stays behind.[/*]
[/list]
